WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:13,140
If my AFP is still elevated, this is a tumor marker.

00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:18,140
After we remove the tumors, what is elevated it?

00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:24,140
So, your tumor markers, remember.

00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:27,140
So, first of all, all the tumor marker tests,

00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:30,140
all the tumor marker tests are just physiological tests.

00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:33,140
They're not only produced by tumors.

00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:36,140
Otherwise, if you don't have any cancer,

00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:41,140
they'd all be zero. They're never zero. There's a normal range.

00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:46,140
So, it's never going to go down to zero.

00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:49,140
And you don't want to.

00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,140
Other things in your body make that chemical.

00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:57,140
It's just found that growing tumors tend to make that specific chemical

00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,140
in greater concentration.

00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:02,140
Therefore, you could use it as a marker of cancerous growth.

00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:06,140
If you have solely a breast tumor, let's say,

00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:10,140
and you remove your breast, and there's no metastasis anywhere else

00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:13,140
by any visual needs that we can tell with the PET skin.

00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:17,140
And you still show elevated tumor markers after you have the breast removed.

00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:20,140
Why are you still showing elevated tumor markers?

00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:25,140
Well, the answer is, I don't know for sure.

00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:28,140
Could it be that you have hidden metastasis?

00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:30,140
That is a possibility.

00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:33,140
Remember, even on a PET scan, remember we said,

00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:36,140
no test is perfect. And even with a PET scan,

00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:41,140
you have to have cancerous mass of over three million cells large

00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:44,140
to even show up positive on a PET scan.

00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:49,140
So, there is a possibility that there is still some metastasis in the body.

00:01:49,140 --> 00:01:55,140
There's a possibility that maybe other cells are producing that tumor marker

00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:58,140
and a greater concentration than our cancerous.

00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:02,140
So, we just don't know, maybe it's going to take some time for that to go down.

00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:07,140
Somebody asked me a question similar to this a while back several months ago

00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:11,140
that they're, because they're tumor marker, how long does it take for tumor markers to go down?

00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:15,140
And I said, well, I have just seen in practice that sometimes it takes a while,

00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:19,140
even after you're out of chemo or after you're doing the right thing,

00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:21,140
the tumor marker still stays elevated.

00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:25,140
And the question was to think the following week, well, why would that be?

00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:27,140
And this is very confusing.

00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:30,140
This is why none of these tests are perfect.

00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:36,140
So, this is why, honestly, this is why a lot of oncologists have stopped using tumor markers

00:02:36,140 --> 00:02:40,140
because if you're going to do what they tell you to do, which is do the chemotherapy,

00:02:40,140 --> 00:02:42,140
lots of times that makes the tumor marker go up.

00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:50,140
So, if you kill the tumors effectively with, what's called something that will cause cell lysis,

00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:53,140
then it can actually spill more of the tumor marker out.

00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:58,140
And you could elevate it and the patient goes free, because they, they, they, they, hey,

00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:02,140
I agreed to do this chemo and I'm getting worse according to the tumor marker test.

00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:07,140
So, they've cut a lot of oncologists just don't do those. That's why I have to ask for them.

00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:11,140
So, there isn't the perfect science to any of this.

00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:17,140
And we get frustrated with science, but the truth is it's nothing is perfect.

00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:22,140
And we don't have a perfect way to see inside your body knows exactly what's going on.

00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:26,140
So, hopefully it's going to go down. That's what we wanted to go down.

